---
source: crates/pse-host/src/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"-h\\n{short}\\n--help\\n{long}\")"
---
-h
Explain selected binary, JSON or textproto payloads without invoking an RPC

Usage: pse inspect payload [OPTIONS] --descriptor <DESCRIPTOR> --message <MESSAGE> --input <INPUT> --encoding <ENCODING>

Options:
  -C <checkout>

      --max-descriptor-bytes <MAX_DESCRIPTOR_BYTES>
          Maximum complete original descriptor artifact bytes [default: 67108864]
      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations [env: PSE_FORMAT] [default: auto] [possible values: auto, human, json, ndjson]
      --max-input-bytes <MAX_INPUT_BYTES>
          Maximum complete original payload bytes, in the selected input grammar [default: 67108864]
      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated literal top-level payload names (for example records). Dots and slashes do not navigate nested data; schema shows valid choices
      --max-converted-bytes <MAX_CONVERTED_BYTES>
          Maximum binary output bytes collected from textproto conversion [default: 67108864]
      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts
      --max-binary-element-bytes <MAX_BINARY_ELEMENT_BYTES>
          Maximum materialized element bytes per descriptor or payload binary decode [default: 33554432]
      --binary-recursion-limit <BINARY_RECURSION_LIMIT>
          Maximum nested messages per descriptor or payload binary decode [default: 100]
      --descriptor <DESCRIPTOR>
          Complete descriptor-set artifact
      --message <MESSAGE>
          Fully qualified message within that artifact
      --input <INPUT>
          Original payload artifact
      --encoding <ENCODING>
          Explicit input grammar [possible values: binary, json, textproto]
      --depth <DEPTH>
          Nested message expansion depth [default: 2]
      --limit <LIMIT>
          Maximum members shown per message or collection [default: 20]
      --original
          Include the exact original input bytes as base64
  -h, --help
          Print help (see more with '--help')
--help
Explain selected binary, JSON or textproto payloads without invoking an RPC

Usage: pse inspect payload [OPTIONS] --descriptor <DESCRIPTOR> --message <MESSAGE> --input <INPUT> --encoding <ENCODING>

Options:
  -C <checkout>


      --max-descriptor-bytes <MAX_DESCRIPTOR_BYTES>
          Maximum complete original descriptor artifact bytes

          [default: 67108864]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Human for a terminal, JSON for pipes
          - human:  Concise summary and pretty structured detail
          - json:   One JSON envelope
          - ndjson: Compact normalized records followed by an observation summary

          [env: PSE_FORMAT]
          [default: auto]

      --max-input-bytes <MAX_INPUT_BYTES>
          Maximum complete original payload bytes, in the selected input grammar

          [default: 67108864]

      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated literal top-level payload names (for example records). Dots and slashes do not navigate nested data; schema shows valid choices

      --max-converted-bytes <MAX_CONVERTED_BYTES>
          Maximum binary output bytes collected from textproto conversion

          [default: 67108864]

      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts

      --max-binary-element-bytes <MAX_BINARY_ELEMENT_BYTES>
          Maximum materialized element bytes per descriptor or payload binary decode

          [default: 33554432]

      --binary-recursion-limit <BINARY_RECURSION_LIMIT>
          Maximum nested messages per descriptor or payload binary decode

          [default: 100]

      --descriptor <DESCRIPTOR>
          Complete descriptor-set artifact

      --message <MESSAGE>
          Fully qualified message within that artifact

      --input <INPUT>
          Original payload artifact

      --encoding <ENCODING>
          Explicit input grammar

          Possible values:
          - binary:    Protocol buffer wire bytes
          - json:      Schema-qualified protobuf JSON
          - textproto: Protobuf text format parsed by native protoc

      --depth <DEPTH>
          Nested message expansion depth

          [default: 2]

      --limit <LIMIT>
          Maximum members shown per message or collection

          [default: 20]

      --original
          Include the exact original input bytes as base64

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
